      "text": "To determine how many positive integers less than 1992 are not factorial tails, we first need to identify the number of trailing zeroes in $m!$ for various values of $m$ and then find how many of these trailing zeroes do not appear as trailing zeroes in $2!$, $3!$, $4!$, and so on until $9!$.\n\nEvery 5, $10=5^2$, 25, etc. factorial prefixes with a 5. Thus, $m$ trailing zeroes in $m!$ can only occur when the numbers in the sequence of preceding numbers divide $m$ as $5^k$ for some nonnegative integer $k$.\n\nWe know that $1! = 1$, $2! = 2$, $3! = 6$, $4! = 24$, $5! = 120$, $6! = 720$, $7! = 5040$, $8! = 40320$, $9! = 362880$, $10! = 3628800\\ldots$ are the major factorial numbers with up to 6 trailing zeroes.\n\nWe can see that any $m$ beginning with a 7 should not have a trailing zero, due to the sequence of numbers only having a 5 followed by a product of a power of 2.\n\nTherefore, ahead of $17$ (given $5^6 = 15625$), we have skipped numbers with trailing zeroes, and that pattern continues, skipping well over 1900 numbers. Since there are 1992 positive integers less than 1992, there are not any factorial tails less than 1992.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
